nel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=1`) — measure the ENFORCING row on a host that has the sysctl set to 1, or route the AppArmor axis to a short SPIKE before committing the lane.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.364,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Two independent mechanisms deny the namespace, and BOTH must be cleared: 1. Ubuntu 23.10+ AppArmor sets kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=1 ... 2. Container runtimes' default seccomp blocks the clone/unshare outright'","Plan measured table: 'Measured on ubuntu:24.04 (bubblewrap 0.9.0)' varies only the container security mode (default / seccomp=unconfined / --privileged) — it does not record the HOST sysctl state under which the row was taken","AppArmor's apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns is a host-kernel sysctl distinct from the container's seccomp profile; a privileged container clearing seccomp does not by itself demonstrate the host AppArmor restriction was present-and-bypassed","Evidence class for the AppArmor axis: Partially-verified (the --privileged capability exists and clears seccomp, but the specific 'clears mechanism #1' surface is unconfirmed)"],"finding":"The plan asserts BOTH namespace-denial mechanisms must be cleared (AppArmor sysctl #1 and container seccomp #2), but the measured ENFORCING result under `--privileged` does not state whether the measurement host had `kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=1` active — so the claim that `--privileged` clears mechanism #1 is unverified; the table may only demonstrate clearing mechanism #2 (seccomp).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbfb42485db096487","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Sections 'The environment precondition, measured' and 'Approach'","norm_id":"n52d728b97bb0d7de","priority":0.536,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A GitHub-hosted runner whose host kernel enforces apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=1 runs the privileged lane; if --privileged does NOT bypass the host AppArmor restriction, bwrap still fails to namespace and the liveness probe fails the lane — or worse, if the runner host does not set the sysctl at all, the lane passes without ever proving the AppArmor axis is handled."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In 'The environment precondition, measured', record the host sysctl value for each table row (e.g. run `sysctl kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns` before the bwrap write) so the ENFORCING result demonstrably exercises mechanism #1, not only seccomp; if that host state cannot be arranged in the measurement environment, mark the AppArmor axis Unverified and gate the lane behind a SPIKE that confirms --privileged bypasses the restriction.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Capture the privileged-container-lane decision and the skip-to-fail flag semantics in an ADR / AGENTS.md update (why --privileged over seccomp-unconfined, why the host sysctl is only a fallback, the flag name and where it is set).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5672,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Adds a new pipeline stage: 'A privileged container lane'","Introduces a new contract: 'an env flag that turns the @live skip into a hard requirement'","DoD lists only 'make lint, make typecheck' with no doc-capture deliverable","The rationale ('--privileged is a plain OCI runtime capability... project.portability requires') and the fallback caveat live only in this plan, not in a durable design record"],"finding":"The plan introduces a novel CI contract — a privileged-container gating lane plus an env flag that flips the @live skip into a hard failure — but does not capture the decision (why privileged is required, why the host sysctl is only a fallback, what the flag is named and where it is set) in any ADR / AGENTS.md / design-doc update.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffcba5e133dd53c1c","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Definition of Done","norm_id":"n13ac7cae884c3836","priority":0.3828,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer sees the privileged lane, doesn't know why unconfined seccomp was insufficient, and 'simplifies' it back to a plain container — silently re-breaking enforcement","Someone adds a new Linux lane unaware the skip-to-fail flag exists and why"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a DoD bullet: record an ADR (or AGENTS.md note) documenting the privileged-container requirement, the mandatory liveness probe, and the requirement-flag name/scope.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Weigh the minimal-privilege prior art (custom seccomp profile allowing clone/unshare + CAP_SYS_ADMIN, or a Podman-style permissive seccomp) against full --privileged, and record why --privileged is chosen over it (e.g., measured/unmeasured, portability, simplicity).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'A privileged container lane. --privileged is a plain OCI runtime capability' with only 'sudo sysctl ... =0' offered as fallback","Retrieved: bubblewrap issue #505 / gitmemories — 'Podman's seccomp filter is more permissive. Bubblewrap works ... in an unprivileged Podman container'","Retrieved: StackOverflow TIL 23443c60 — the blocker is Docker's default seccomp on unshare(CLONE_NEWUSER), implying a targeted seccomp allowance rather than full privilege can suffice","Security/privilege-escalation bright-line: --privileged grants all capabilities + disables seccomp/AppArmor, a broader grant than the minimal set bwrap needs"],"finding":"The plan commits to full container --privileged as the enforcement mechanism without considering the documented less-privileged prior art (a custom seccomp profile permitting clone/unshare combined with CAP_SYS_ADMIN, or a more-permissive default seccomp as under Podman) that lets bwrap create user namespaces without granting the container all capabilities.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8a03f816dba03357","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section","norm_id":"ncfbe765878828bf2","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or security policy that forbids --privileged CI containers asks why a narrower CAP_SYS_ADMIN + custom-seccomp lane was not chosen","A self-hosted runner where --privileged is disallowed but capability additions are permitted"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a row or note to the measured table for a targeted grant (e.g., --cap-add SYS_ADMIN with a seccomp profile that unblocks clone/unshare), or state explicitly that this narrower mechanism was considered and deferred as unmeasured — mirroring the honest treatment already given to the sysctl fallback.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"0d21c0cdcd31bacf","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["074b1366aff474a7",3899],"description_boxes":["7879981d4f226a8f",0],"file_impact":["a661f51cf8464980",2],